# Keeps the Docker build context small and, more importantly, makes sure
# `.env` (and anything else that must never be baked into an image layer)
# can never be picked up by a `COPY . .`-style instruction even if one is
# added later. apps/gateway/Dockerfile currently COPYs explicit paths, not
# `.`, but this file is the backstop regardless of how the Dockerfile
# evolves — see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md's "Segredos" section for why secrets
# are injected at runtime (env vars) and never at build time.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
build/
**/build/
coverage/
**/coverage/
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.git/
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
docs/
